title: Ethersphere bee-js / Swarm Desktop Malware Stage C2 (api.frameworkmetrics.xyz)
id: b147957b-700c-4b19-b4db-1040a1417ecc
status: experimental
description: Detects web requests to api.frameworkmetrics.xyz, the second-stage host contacted by the malicious @ethersphere/bee-js 13.3.0 npm postinstall loader and the Swarm Desktop 0.56.2 build published in the November 2026 Ethersphere release-pipeline compromise. The loader POSTs stolen config.yaml and data-dir/keys/swarm.key material to the /v1/analytics, /v1/electron and /v1/swarm/report endpoints.
references:
  - https://www.ox.security/blog/ethersphere-hijacked-with-crypto-stealing-malware-via-github-npm
  - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/hackers-compromise-etherspheres-bee-js.html
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/10
tags:
  - attack.t1195
  - attack.t1105
  - attack.t1552
  - attack.t1041
logsource:
  category: proxy
detection:
  selection_host:
    cs-host|endswith: 'frameworkmetrics.xyz'
  condition: selection_host
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely — the host is dedicated attacker infrastructure; an unrelated service legitimately named frameworkmetrics.xyz would be the only way to trip this
level: critical
